{text:"Fix a smooth real mean-zero initial datum and an arbitrary positive integer L. H001 makes tau=T/L>0. The update preserves smoothness by its products, inverse derivatives and Airy multipliers. Its first and all projected terms have mean zero; the mean of the second H_tau term vanishes because S_tau Dinv f has mean zero. Conjugate symmetry is preserved by real products, real differential operators and the Airy group, so the iterates are real. Induction establishes these properties at every grid point. E004 applied at each f=v^n gives exactly v^{n+1}=f+F_n(t_{n+1})+C_n(t_{n+1})-R2(f,f,f). In V the Q_n endpoint and its occurrence in W_n cancel. Thus V(t_n)=f and V(t_{n+1})=v^{n+1}, proving continuity between steps. Differentiating its smooth step integrals gives F_n'=B_t(f,f)/2 and V'=B_t(f+F_n,f+F_n)/2-W_n/tau. Subtract F_n' to get the claimed Y_n' and note Y_n(t_n)=0. The construction is spatially smooth and piecewise time-smooth, as claimed.",uses:["H001","E004"]}
